{
  "_comment": [
    "Campaign 03 does two jobs.",
    "",
    "JOB 1 -- CONFIRM WHAT CAMPAIGN 02 DISCOVERED. Campaign 02 found that `Win`",
    "from autoexec.con leaves the process running at the 120 s deadline while",
    "the identical probe with `Lose` exits in ~13 s. That claim was DISCOVERED,",
    "not predicted: the registered prediction Q1 expected the Win arm to pass,",
    "and refute.py returned REFUTED on exactly that mismatch. Correctly. A claim",
    "born from a surprise has been tested by nothing. So it is registered here,",
    "in advance, and re-run.",
    "",
    "JOB 2 -- THE BAKE PIPELINE, which is now the top of the board. A parallel",
    "lane measured that a statically-linked D3DX9 block occupies roughly",
    "0x00570000-0x005c8000: below it 57.99% of bytes are observed, above it",
    "8.50%, and the .rdata carries DDERR_ x113, JFIF x7, PNG/zlib/inflate and",
    "D3DX x15. Most of the CFastVB/CDXTexture dark mass -- the largest prize a",
    "byte-ranked selector points at -- is Microsoft's code, and lighting it",
    "teaches nothing about Aquila. What IS Aquila, and IS dark, is a content-bake",
    "pipeline shipped inside the retail exe, and two of its entry points are",
    "console commands sitting in the same 33-entry table as Win and Lose:",
    "BuildStaticShadows (0x004ebbb0) and BuildLandscapeCache (0x00544700).",
    "",
    "PREDICTIONS, REGISTERED IN ADVANCE. This commit precedes the first launch.",
    "",
    "W1  winconf reports FAIL 3/3 with self-exit rate 0.0 -- no replicate exits",
    "    on its own before the deadline.",
    "    FALSIFIED BY: any winconf replicate self-exiting. That kills the",
    "    campaign-02 claim outright.",
    "",
    "W2  loseconf reports PASS 3/3 with self-exit rate 1.0.",
    "    FALSIFIED BY: any loseconf replicate failing to exit. That would make",
    "    the campaign-02 contrast a coincidence of two small samples.",
    "",
    "B1  THE ONE THAT DECIDES CAMPAIGN STRATEGY. BuildStaticShadows and",
    "    BuildLandscapeCache do their work SYNCHRONOUSLY inside the command, so",
    "    the before/after MemStats pair DIFFERS in at least one of the shadows,",
    "    landscape or texture-cache lines.",
    "    EXPECTED UNDER SYNCHRONOUS: before != after, byte level.",
    "    EXPECTED UNDER DEFERRED-TO-A-TICK: byte-identical, exactly as every",
    "    single one of the 9 arms in campaign 02 came back.",
    "    FALSIFIED BY: byte-identical before/after.",
    "    WHY IT MATTERS MORE THAN THE OTHER TWO: campaign 02 established that all",
    "    autoexec lines are dispatched in one burst before the simulation ticks.",
    "    If a console command cannot do synchronous work, then no console probe",
    "    can ever light up dark code, and the entire unattended lever is worth",
    "    only what the level load itself executes. If it can, the bake pipeline",
    "    is reachable tonight and 69,490 dark GAME bytes are addressable without",
    "    elevation.",
    "",
    "B2  shadows and landscape both report PASS 3/3 -- the command after them",
    "    runs and the process still exits.",
    "    FALSIFIED BY: either arm failing to exit, which would make them behave",
    "    like Win rather than like Lose and would be a finding in itself.",
    "",
    "SCOPE. Level 100 only. No coverage: TTD needs elevation, this campaign does",
    "not use it, and no statement about which functions executed is possible",
    "from it. B1 is about a memory-report delta, which is evidence that WORK",
    "happened, not evidence about which code did it."
  ],
  "probes": [
    {
      "name": "winconf-r1",
      "level": 100,
      "sourceRoot": "../../local-lab/safe-copy-bea-pristine",
      "makeDirs": ["data/Memory"],
      "autoexec": ["Echo C03-WIN", "MemStats c3_before.txt", "Win", "MemStats c3_after.txt", "Quit"],
      "oracle": { "kind": "all", "timeoutSeconds": 120, "settleSeconds": 5,
        "of": [ { "kind": "fileAppears", "path": "data/Memory/c3_after.txt", "minBytes": 1024 }, { "kind": "processExit" } ] },
      "collect": ["data/Memory/c3_before.txt", "data/Memory/c3_after.txt"]
    },
    {
